<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Quantity over Quality: Believing that listing many technologies is better than deep evaluation. (IB Feedback: "better responses provided a balanced account").</li>
        <li>Ethics vs. Logic: Weaker responses often drift into purely ethical debate without addressing the underlying computational complexity or hardware constraints.</li>
        <li>Isolation: Forgetting that the Case Study is part of the CS curriculum; students must link findings to specific syllabus content (e.g., how vSLAM uses Matrix math or ADTs).</li>
    </ul>
</div>

